CAT = "nzreDiscipline"; SEG = "DIS"
Q = [
("Work that falls short of what a member of the public may expect from a reasonably competent licensee is:",
 "Unsatisfactory conduct", ["Serious misconduct", "A civil mistake only", "A breach of the Code only"],
 "Section 72 of the Real Estate Agents Act 2008 defines unsatisfactory conduct to include work below the standard a reasonable member of the public may expect from a reasonably competent licensee."),
("Which of these is a ground of unsatisfactory conduct under section 72?",
 "Breaching a rule under the Act", ["Taking a day of annual leave", "Working for two agents at once", "Declining a new listing offer"],
 "Section 72 also covers incompetent or negligent work, work agents of good standing would find unacceptable, and any contravention of the Act, regulations or rules."),
("Conduct that agents of good standing, or reasonable members of the public, would regard as disgraceful is:",
 "Misconduct", ["Unsatisfactory conduct", "A technical breach only", "Poor customer service"],
 "Section 73 defines misconduct to include conduct reasonably regarded as disgraceful, seriously incompetent or negligent agency work, and wilful or reckless contravention of the Act or rules."),
("A licensee knowingly ignores a rule on disclosure to win a listing. Which level of conduct best fits a wilful contravention?",
 "Misconduct", ["Unsatisfactory conduct", "Neither, it is a business choice", "A disagreement for the courts"],
 "Wilful or reckless contravention of the Act, other Acts that apply to licensees, or the rules is misconduct under section 73."),
("A conviction can amount to misconduct when the offence:",
 "Reflects badly on their fitness", ["Was committed in the last month", "Involved a motor vehicle only", "Was committed overseas only"],
 "Section 73 includes an offence for which the licensee has been convicted that reflects adversely on their fitness to be a licensee."),
("Who may complain about a licensee's conduct?",
 "Any person, in writing", ["Only a client of the licensee", "Only another licensee", "Only the buyer or seller"],
 "Section 74 allows any person to complain in writing to the Authority about a licensee's conduct."),
("The Registrar may decide not to pursue a complaint that:",
 "Raises an inconsequential issue", ["Names a salesperson, not an agent", "Arrives after a settlement date", "Comes from a business competitor"],
 "Section 74(3) lets the Registrar decide a complaint need not be pursued if it is inconsequential, frivolous or vexatious, better referred elsewhere, or already resolved to the complainant's satisfaction."),
("Which body hears a charge of misconduct and can cancel a licence?",
 "The Disciplinary Tribunal", ["A Complaints Committee", "The Registrar's office", "The agency's own manager"],
 "The Disciplinary Tribunal hears charges of misconduct and may make orders including cancelling or suspending a licence (sections 100 and 110)."),
("For how long at most can the Disciplinary Tribunal suspend a licence for misconduct?",
 "24 months", ["6 months", "12 months", "5 years"],
 "Section 110(2)(c) allows an order suspending a licensee's licence for a period not exceeding 24 months."),
("A Complaints Assessment Committee finds unsatisfactory conduct. Which order may it make?",
 "Order extra training", ["Cancel the licence now", "Imprison the licensee", "Suspend the agent's company"],
 "Under section 93 a Committee may censure, require an apology, order training, reduce or refund fees, require errors rectified, fine, and refer a matter to the Tribunal for compensation. Cancellation is a Tribunal order."),
("A Committee finds a licensee failed to complete work properly. Which order helps the complainant directly?",
 "Fix the error at their own cost", ["Publish an apology in the media", "Surrender the licence for a year", "Take over the agency's accounts"],
 "Section 93(1)(f) lets a Committee order a licensee to rectify any error or omission at their own expense, or provide relief where that is not practicable."),
("The Tribunal finds misconduct by a salesperson. Besides suspension or cancellation, it may order that the salesperson:",
 "Not be engaged in agency work", ["Hand the client a free valuation", "Repeat the course at their cost", "Pay a bonus to the complainant"],
 "Section 110(2)(e) allows an order that any current employment or engagement be terminated and that no agent employ or engage the person in connection with agency work."),
("On what standard must the Tribunal be satisfied that a charge is proved?",
 "The balance of probabilities", ["Beyond all reasonable doubt", "Only reasonable suspicion", "The complainant's own belief"],
 "Section 110(1) says the Tribunal must be satisfied the charge is proved on the balance of probabilities."),
("Under rule 12.1, what must an agent have in place for complaints?",
 "Written complaint procedures", ["A verbal promise to resolve it", "A standard refund policy", "A letter from the Registrar"],
 "Rule 12.1 requires an agent to develop and maintain written in-house procedures for complaints and dispute resolution, available to clients and consumers."),
("A customer is unhappy about a salesperson. Under rule 12.3 the customer may complain to the Authority:",
 "Without using in-house steps first", ["Only after in-house steps fail", "Only through the agent's office", "Only after waiting 12 months"],
 "Rule 12.3 says licensees must make sure people know they can use the Authority's complaints process without first using the agency's procedures."),
("A salesperson learns of a complaint to the Authority about their work. Under rule 12.4, they must tell their agent within:",
 "10 working days", ["One working day", "5 working days", "30 calendar days"],
 "Rule 12.4 requires a licensee employed or engaged by an agent to advise the agent within 10 working days of becoming aware of a complaint, a Committee decision or order, and any later Tribunal decision."),
]
